id: pm-hnc9w7
title: "Graph wave: changelog-safe legacy edge hygiene batch — retire the no-active-blocker sentinel, duplicate spellings, terminal ordering cycles, and dangling terminal references"
description: "Execute a dedicated changelog-safe cleanup of legacy graph sentinels, duplicate relationship spellings, terminal ordering cycles, and dangling terminal references."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[7]: batch,changelog-safe,cleanup,governance,graph,legacy,relationships
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:48:07.339Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-29T21:22:32.435Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: "The no-active-blocker sentinel references are removed from all holders; blocker state derives from real edges only; Duplicated parent and child spellings between terminal endpoints collapse to the canonical single spelling; Terminal-only ordering cycles are broken by dropping the single lowest-evidence edge per cycle, with the choice recorded; Dangling terminal references to absent items are resolved or removed with the rationale recorded on the holder; The changelog effect is measured before and after; regeneration runs as the last step and any bucket movement is stated explicitly in the batch record; pm graph audit reports zero findings for all four legacy codes after the batch"
goal: explainable-graph
objective: The audit reports zero legacy findings without dragging closed items into a release changelog
value: "One hundred and fifty-eight terminal items carry edges that mean nothing: a retired sentinel, duplicated parent and child spellings of the same relationship, ordering cycles between closed milestones, and references to items that never existed. Every graph traversal and every audit run pays to skip them."
impact: Removes the permanent noise floor from graph governance so that a non-zero audit finding count becomes actionable again instead of expected.
outcome: "The audit's four legacy codes report zero, executed as one deliberate batch whose changelog effect is controlled and stated up front."
why_now: "The audit itself names the remediation as a dedicated changelog-safe closed-item batch and explicitly forbids ad hoc repair. That batch has never been scheduled, so the findings recur on every run."
parent: pm-a8zm
